englishTranslation:
Masks have fallen off faces, deep scars remain;
The illusion shatters today, I am frightened by the truth;
I do not sing songs.

Who is the Kaurava, who is the Pandava?
A crooked question;
Kurukshetra on both sides, mortality on both flanks.

Do not wander to Manali, my fair one!
A sheet of snow awaits, but the mountain sun is fierce;
Lest your heart lose itself in deodar forests.

text:
Where the mind is without fear and the head is held high;
Where knowledge is free;
Where the world has not been broken up into fragments
By narrow domestic walls;
Into that heaven of freedom, my Father, let my country awake.
